:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325227}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d16d4609-6b42-5a5b-a115-183074533c0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-135394" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the following matrix:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we're given a Frobenius matrix:\n\n- all entries on the main diagonal are ones\n\n- the matrix has only one column (the $1$st column) where some entries below the main diagonal are not zeros\n\n- all the other entries outside the main diagonal are zeros\n\nTo find the inverse of a Frobenius matrix, we simply take the non-zero entries outside the main diagonal with opposite signs. \n\nIn our case, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3} & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367655 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "77673d0c-9f03-5915-b2ab-4a5d6cb2d94d" :knowledge-point/title "Inverting a Frobenius Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b3e496f-43a3-5939-9b6e-cda114464504" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367657} {:answer/id #uuid "06aa3be6-dc87-5c1f-9157-e8cf726ba8c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -\\sqrt{2} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367658} {:answer/id #uuid "f61e1485-0570-5403-8490-33deccfbaad2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 &